  "text": "Firstly, since $|-a|=|a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n12q-|2q|.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12q-|2q| & = \\\\ 12q-|2|\\cdot |q| & = \\\\ 12q-2\\cdot |q| & = \\\\ 12q-2|q| & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $q\\ge 0,$ we have that $|q|=q.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12q-2|q| & = \\\\ 12q-2q & = \\\\ 10q & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14183863/history-expanded-3018a614de486e28aac1.html",
